488: 		<h1>Changelog</h1>
489: <p>All notable user-facing changes to cast, newest first.</p>
490: <h2>0.12.6</h2>
491: <h3>Fixed</h3>
492: <ul>
493: <li><code>grep</code>: the built-in JS fallback (used when ripgrep isn&#39;t on <code>PATH</code>) failed to find matches when the search path named a single file instead of a directory — it called <code>readdir()</code> on the file and silently swallowed the resulting <code>ENOTDIR</code>. The ripgrep-backed path already handled this case; the fallback now does too.</li>
494: <li>Plan mode&#39;s read-only command check rejected safe commands like <code>ls -la 2&gt;&amp;1</code> or <code>cmd &gt;/dev/null 2&gt;&amp;1</code> — fd-duplication and null-device redirects were caught by the blanket output-redirection guard even though neither writes a persistent file.</li>
495: <li><code>bash</code>: background tasks (<code>run_in_background: true</code>) no longer get killed by a default timeout — they&#39;re open-ended by default (dev servers, long builds) and only get a kill timer when the model explicitly passes <code>timeout</code>. A <code>timeout</code> of <code>0</code> or negative is treated as &quot;no timeout&quot; rather than firing almost immediately.</li>
496: <li><code>/continue</code> and starting a new session now restore the full session state (reasoning settings, turn metadata, title, pinned flag, todos, share token) instead of a partial subset, and reset SSH host resolution and provider/model validation consistently when switching sessions or projects.</li>
497: </ul>
498: <h2>0.12.5</h2>
499: <h3>Fixed</h3>
500: <ul>
501: <li>Planning flow: complex build-mode tasks now consistently request planning before implementation, while an explicit user choice to continue in Build is preserved across subsequent turns.</li>
502: <li>Web UI: plan-mode entry and plan approval now use the same choices as the terminal UI, including refine, immediate implementation, fresh-context implementation, and manual Build handoff.</li>
503: <li>Web UI: every plan-mode decision is saved as a persistent system card in the chat history, so the selected path remains clear after reload.</li>
504: </ul>
505: <h2>0.12.4</h2>
506: <h3>Fixed</h3>
507: <ul>
508: <li>Web UI: settings remain responsive when adding or removing Skills.sh skills, including when Settings is opened from a fresh root draft with no visible session.</li>
509: <li>Tool output: valid JSON containing Unicode escape sequences now renders as readable text in both the web UI and terminal UI.</li>
510: <li>Web UI: font previews are local and stable, so the picker shows each typeface immediately without late-loading flicker.</li>
511: <li><code>grep</code>: directory-component globs now match relative to the requested search path consistently whether ripgrep is installed or the built-in fallback is used.</li>
512: </ul>
513: <h2>0.12.2</h2>
514: <h3>Fixed</h3>
515: <ul>
516: <li>Web UI: hover tooltips were silently broken on message rows after the mid-word boundary-merge rework — the <code>PAD</code> constant the tooltip layout depended on had been removed alongside the dead hover-cancel code path. Restored; tooltips on user / agent / reasoning rows, tool cards, and MCP tool rows are back.</li>
517: <li>Web UI: when a streaming reply was truncated by <code>max_tokens</code> <em>inside</em> a model-emitted draft answer (i.e. reasoning had already closed and the model was emitting real content for the user when it ran out of budget), the partial answer was being discarded. The last accumulated content is now flushed into its own <code>[agent]</code> block — same way the answer-after-reasoning case was handled in 0.12.1.</li>
518: <li>Web UI: mid-stream mouse movement no longer cancels a hover tooltip before it appears. The previous <code>mousemove</code> → cancel handler kept the tooltip code technically alive but fired on every cursor wiggle and never let the 500ms hover-intent timer complete. Removed; tooltips open on the intended timer and only the standard <code>mouseleave</code> / scroll / modal-open paths dismiss them.</li>
519: <li>Web UI: the browser&#39;s native tooltip is stripped the moment the cursor enters the trigger element. Otherwise both tooltips render and the native one wins the race on leaving the page, briefly showing the plain <code>title</code> text over the styled bubble.</li>
520: <li>Web UI: custom hover tooltips are suppressed on coarse-pointer / touch devices, where they have no interaction model and were firing on tap-and-release.</li>
521: </ul>
522: <h3>Changed</h3>
523: <ul>
524: <li>Built-in <code>cast</code> configuration skill: split the 397-line <code>SKILL.md</code> into a short index + seven <code>references/*.md</code> topic files (personas, skills, marketplace, mcp, rules, hooks, commands). The skill now follows the agentskills.io progressive-disclosure convention — only the frontmatter + topic map (~1.6 KB) is loaded every time <code>cast</code> is invoked for a config question, and the matching reference file is read on demand. For a focused question (e.g. &quot;how do I add an MCP server?&quot;) the model pulls just <code>references/mcp.md</code> instead of every topic.</li>
525: </ul>
526: <h2>0.12.1</h2>
527: <h3>Fixed</h3>
528: <ul>
529: <li>Web UI: when a reasoning block ended with a markdown heading (a truncated answer draft that the parser flushed into reasoning because the model ran out of <code>max_tokens</code> inside <code>&lt;think&gt;</code> without emitting a close tag), the post-heading tail is now rendered as a separate <code>[agent]</code> block instead of sitting inside <code>[reasoning]</code> next to a blank agent area. Applies to live streaming, settled turns, and reload from disk.</li>
530: <li>Web UI: when the model&#39;s <code>&lt;think&gt;...&lt;/think&gt;</code> boundary landed <em>mid-word</em> (observed on MiniMax-M3 emitting <code>&lt;/think&gt;</code> inside the Cyrillic word &quot;Сейчас&quot;, so reasoning ended &quot;...Сей&quot; and content started &quot;час уточню...&quot;), the trailing word fragment is now glued back onto the agent&#39;s content. The user sees the model-intended continuous word — &quot;Сейчас уточню текущую погоду в Астане.&quot; — instead of two halves separated across blocks. Same-script check (Latin↔Latin, Cyrillic↔Cyrillic) guards against false merges across alphabets; sentence-ending punctuation inside the fragment stays in reasoning.</li>
531: </ul>
532: <h2>0.12.0</h2>
533: <h3>Added</h3>
534: <ul>
535: <li><p><strong>Per-persona allowlists</strong> for tools, skills, MCP servers, and subagent types. Each persona&#39;s frontmatter now supports four knobs that all share the same shape (omitted = no restriction, <code>[]</code> = explicitly nothing allowed, exact names or <code>*</code>-globs):</p>
536: <ul>
537: <li><code>tools:</code> — built-in tool names (existing). <code>tools: [read, grep, ls, plan_*, web_*]</code> narrows the persona&#39;s builtin reach.</li>
538: <li><code>skills:</code> — skill names invokable via the <code>skill</code> tool. <code>skills: [research, deep-research]</code> hides every other skill from the catalog and the runtime.</li>
539: <li><code>mcp:</code> — MCP <strong>server</strong> names (not individual tool names). <code>mcp: [postgres, playwright*]</code> keeps only those servers&#39; tools callable.</li>
540: <li><code>subagentTypes:</code> — narrows <code>subagents: true</code> further. <code>subagentTypes: [explore, review]</code> is the only set this persona can spawn via <code>task</code>.</li>
541: </ul>
542: <p>Enforced at runtime (not just in the prompt text) — a disallowed call gets the same &quot;not available&quot; / &quot;not found&quot; / &quot;Unknown subagent&quot; message the model already gets for any hidden tool, so these actually isolate a persona&#39;s zone of responsibility. <code>skills:</code> / <code>mcp:</code> restrictions also forward to anything the persona delegates to via <code>task</code>, so the restriction can&#39;t be routed around by spawning a subagent.</p>
543: <p>Default persona is now <code>senior</code> (the previous <code>coding</code> persona was a strict subset and is removed). <code>coder-with-subagents-force-review</code> is also removed — its review gate now lives in <code>coder-with-subagents</code>&#39;s own validation pattern.</p>
544: </li>
545: </ul>
546: <h2>0.11.1</h2>
547: <h3>Fixed</h3>
548: <ul>
549: <li><code>cast web &lt;typo of stop|status&gt;</code> no longer silently starts a new server daemon — any unrecognized subcommand now errors instead of falling through to the default &quot;start&quot; behavior.</li>
550: <li><code>cast upgrade --&lt;typo of --force&gt;</code> no longer silently attempts to upgrade to a &quot;version&quot; named after the mistyped flag — unknown flags now error before that logic runs.</li>
551: <li><code>/ssh &lt;typo of add|remove&gt;</code> (terminal UI) no longer silently falls back to listing hosts — unrecognized subcommands now error.</li>
552: </ul>
553: <h2>0.11.0</h2>
554: <h3>Fixed</h3>
555: <ul>
556: <li>Skills.sh: installing via the web UI now actually lands where cast scans (<code>~/.agents/skills/</code>) — installs used to silently vanish depending on which agent flag was used.</li>
557: <li>Skills.sh: pasting skills.sh&#39;s own &quot;npx skills add ...&quot; command into the install field now works, not just the bare <code>owner/repo --skill name</code> args.</li>
558: <li>Skills.sh: the installed-skill list now shows the real source repo (read from the skills.sh lockfile) instead of a mis-parsed label that was always empty.</li>
559: <li>Skills.sh / SSH: command output no longer leaks raw ANSI escape codes (cursor show/hide sequences) into the UI.</li>
560: <li>Settings modal: a failed action no longer leaves every button in the modal permanently disabled.</li>
561: <li>Diff/Files panel: a manually resized width now survives a page reload.</li>
562: <li>Hooks: a hook that force-stops the turn no longer silently drops <code>updatedInput</code>/<code>additionalContext</code> contributed by other hooks in the same run.</li>
563: <li>Hooks: a <code>PostToolUse</code>/<code>PostToolUseFailure</code> hook that blocks with no output of its own no longer has its block silently dropped.</li>
564: <li>Hooks: two identical hook groups from different sources (e.g. a plugin and a project file) no longer share an id, so disabling one no longer disables the other.</li>
565: <li>Hooks: a malformed <code>hooks.json</code> now surfaces a parse-error diagnostic in Settings and <code>/hooks</code> instead of silently loading as empty.</li>
566: </ul>
567: <h3>Changed</h3>
568: <ul>
569: <li>Web UI: Marketplace tab browsing merged into one flat, searchable list across all configured marketplaces instead of per-marketplace tabs.</li>
570: <li>Web UI: Skills.sh tab dropped the &quot;list available&quot; (browse-a-repo) field and the network-backed search box.</li>
571: </ul>
572: <h2>0.10.1</h2>
573: <h3>Fixed</h3>
574: <ul>
575: <li>Hooks: <code>${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}</code> substitution in command strings so plugins shipped with Claude Code&#39;s marketplace (e.g. hookify, ralph-loop) load and execute unmodified.</li>
576: <li>Hooks: case-insensitive tool-name matching in <code>if</code> conditions so <code>if: &quot;Bash(git commit:*)&quot;</code> matches payloads where the tool name is lowercase &quot;bash&quot;.</li>
577: <li>Skills: <code>skill</code> tool description in <code>/skill-instructions</code> now explicitly tells the model to call the <code>skill</code> tool (not <code>read</code>) and to load skills FIRST when the request matches a description.</li>
578: <li>Personas: every persona&#39;s Tools section mentions the <code>skill</code> tool with a generic description (no skill-name examples, to avoid locking in a specific subset).</li>
579: </ul>
580: <h3>Changed</h3>
581: <ul>
582: <li>Skills prompt listing now includes <code>whenToUse</code> alongside <code>description</code> (formatted as <code>description — whenToUse</code>) for richer model matching.</li>
583: </ul>
584: <h2>0.10.0</h2>
585: <h3>Added</h3>
586: <ul>
587: <li>Hooks: full implementation matching the Claude Code protocol — shell/HTTP commands fire on lifecycle events to validate/block a tool call, log activity, or keep the agent working before it stops. Configure via <code>.cast/hooks.json</code> (project) or <code>~/.cast/hooks.json</code> (global); manage with <code>/hooks</code>, <code>/hooks enable|disable &lt;id&gt;</code>, <code>/hooks help</code>.</li>
588: <li>Web UI: Settings → Hooks tab, mirroring <code>/hooks</code> (per-source grouping, enable/disable toggle).</li>
589: <li>Skills: dedicated <code>skill</code> tool replaces the model reading <code>SKILL.md</code> via the generic <code>read</code> tool — validates the name, enforces <code>disable-model-invocation</code>, and performs argument substitution in one call.</li>
590: <li>Skills: <code>$ARGUMENTS</code>, <code>$ARGUMENTS[0]</code>/<code>$0</code>, and <code>${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}</code> substitution in skill bodies, plus a <code>when_to_use</code> frontmatter field surfaced in the skill listing as <code>description — whenToUse</code>.</li>
591: <li>Web UI: marketplace tabs with a plugin catalog browser (alphabetically sorted tabs and plugins, full descriptions).</li>
592: </ul>
593: <h3>Changed</h3>
594: <ul>
595: <li>Web UI: Settings panel restyled — MCP/Skills/SSH intro text switched from a collapsible <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> to an always-visible summary line; item rows, plugin catalog entries, and theme/font swatches share a consistent card/hover treatment; Plugins tab renamed to Marketplace, settings tabs sorted alphabetically (opens first tab by default).</li>
596: <li>Web UI: font swatches load their Google Fonts stylesheet so every option previews in its own font instead of falling back to the system font.</li>
597: </ul>
598: <h3>Fixed</h3>
599: <ul>
600: <li>Case-insensitive tool name matching in hook <code>if</code> conditions.</li>
601: <li><code>${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}</code> substitution in hook command strings for plugin compatibility.</li>
602: <li>Hook protocol parity — missing payload fields and output formats now match Claude Code&#39;s.</li>
603: <li>MCP/Skills/SSH settings tabs now work while the agent is running.</li>
604: </ul>
605: <h2>0.9.14</h2>
606: <h3>Fixed</h3>
607: <ul>
608: <li>Vision error fallback now catches 400 status codes in addition to 404, so provider image-rejection errors (e.g. oversized base64) trigger image stripping and retry instead of surfacing a raw 400 to the user.</li>
609: <li>Per-file image read cap lowered from 25MB to 5MB to match provider limits, preventing images from being embedded only to get rejected at the API.</li>
610: </ul>
611: <h2>0.9.13</h2>
612: <h3>Internal</h3>
613: <ul>
614: <li>Zero biome lint warnings/errors project-wide.</li>
615: </ul>
616: <h2>0.9.12</h2>
617: <h3>Changed</h3>
618: <ul>
619: <li><code>todo_write</code> is now guidance-based — the hard gate that blocked non-todo tool calls after 4 work actions is removed. The model decides when to use <code>todo_write</code> based on task complexity, same as opencode&#39;s <code>todowrite</code>.</li>
620: </ul>
621: <h2>0.9.11</h2>
622: <h3>Fixed</h3>
623: <ul>
624: <li>Web UI: the Inputs tab loading state now uses the same &quot;Loading…&quot; style as every other panel instead of an inconsistent title-sized label.</li>
625: </ul>
626: <h2>0.9.10</h2>
627: <h3>Fixed</h3>
628: <ul>
629: <li>Web UI: the Inputs sidebar no longer shows a stale &quot;No files attached&quot; flash when re-fetching after a document upload or during agent-response re-renders.</li>
630: <li>Web UI: attached documents in a draft session (before the first message was sent) now work — the upload is deferred to <code>submitMessage</code> after <code>commitSession</code> creates the real session, instead of blocking with &quot;send a message first&quot;.</li>
631: <li>Web UI: a double <code>commitSession</code> call when drafting a session with pending documents created two separate sessions — files landed in the first, the message in the second, so the Inputs tab was empty while the chat showed the files. A single <code>id</code> variable now flows through both blocks.</li>
632: <li>Web UI: the sidebar&#39;s &quot;No sessions match&quot; empty state no longer flashes during initial load before the session list arrives.</li>
633: </ul>
634: <h3>Changed</h3>
635: <ul>
636: <li>Web UI: tightened chat vertical spacing — smaller gap, leaner padding, and reduced line-height for denser messages.</li>
637: </ul>
638: <h2>0.9.9</h2>
639: <h3>Added</h3>
640: <ul>
641: <li>Session search (TUI and web) now runs on a SQLite FTS5 index over full message history instead of a JS fuzzy scorer — same relevance ranking in both interfaces, and a multi-word query now matches across different messages in the same conversation instead of only within one.</li>
642: <li><code>web_fetch</code> gets a second backend: &quot;local&quot; fetches the URL directly (no third party sees it) and converts HTML itself, with a Cloudflare-challenge retry, a 5MB response cap, and content-type checks that reject binaries. Switch with <code>/web-fetch-provider jina|local</code> (default stays <code>jina</code>).</li>
643: <li>Web UI: an &quot;Inputs&quot; tab (right sidebar, ordered Inputs/Files/Changes) for a session&#39;s attached documents.</li>
644: <li>Web UI: the composer&#39;s attach button now accepts documents, not just images — non-image files upload to a session-scoped directory and the model gets told their path via an invisible reminder on send. Executable/binary formats are rejected; archives and ordinary documents are allowed.</li>
645: <li><code>cast web</code>&#39;s MCP servers now connect in the background after the HTTP server starts listening, instead of blocking startup on every configured server (npx spawns, browser launches, remote handshakes) — the server accepts requests immediately, and connected tools become available in any open session automatically once the connect finishes.</li>
646: </ul>
647: <h3>Changed</h3>
648: <ul>
649: <li>Web UI: the &quot;Tools&quot; settings tab split into three — Bash, Web, Quick Mode — each loading only the data it needs instead of five settings commands on every open.</li>
650: <li><code>web_fetch</code>: one retry on a transient network failure or 5xx (never on an intentional abort or a 4xx), and truncation now prefers the nearest paragraph break over a mid-sentence cut.</li>
651: </ul>
652: <h3>Fixed</h3>
653: <ul>
654: <li><code>web_fetch</code> now rejects non-http(s) URL schemes (<code>file://</code>, <code>data:</code>, ...) before ever making a network call.</li>
655: <li><code>cast web status</code>/&quot;already running&quot; could report a server as up before it was actually accepting connections — the daemon state file is now written only once the HTTP server is truly listening, matching its own documented contract.</li>
656: </ul>
657: <h2>0.9.8</h2>
658: <h3>Fixed</h3>
659: <ul>
660: <li>Web UI: tooltips display as a single horizontal line instead of wrapping into a narrow column due to <code>max-width</code> and <code>word-break</code> constraints.</li>
661: <li>Web UI: <code>assistant_message</code> handler now uses event payload (<code>content</code>/<code>thinking</code>/<code>toolCalls</code>) as fallback when streaming blocks are empty, preventing silently dropped messages on SSE interruptions.</li>
662: </ul>
663: <h2>0.9.7</h2>
664: <h3>Added</h3>
665: <ul>
666: <li>Web UI: custom tooltip system — themed bubbles with fast appearance, viewport-aware positioning, no truncation.</li>
667: <li>Web UI: keyboard shortcuts icon (heroicons-compatible outline style).</li>
668: <li>Web UI: all settings tabs now have collapsible help sections (Model, Tools, MCP, Skills, SSH, Plugins).</li>
669: <li>Web UI: SSH settings now support password authentication (requires <code>sshpass</code>).</li>
670: </ul>
671: <h3>Changed</h3>
672: <ul>
673: <li>Web UI: Settings modal widened from 620px to 820px for better readability.</li>
674: <li>Web UI: help sections in Tools and Model tabs now use inline hints after each section title instead of a single collapsible block.</li>
675: <li>Web UI: theme swatches redesigned with grid layout — dot left-aligned, label centered.</li>
676: <li>Web UI: every theme now carries its own background palette (bg, bgSurface, bgRaised, bgHover, border, borderActive) with improved contrast between UI layers.</li>
677: <li>Web UI: 6 themes (Nord, Solarized, Catppuccin, GitHub, Dracula, Gruvbox) use official background colors from their design specifications.</li>
678: <li>Web UI: reasoning blocks and turn-meta footer now use <code>--text-dim</code> for better readability.</li>
679: <li>Web UI: chevron icon in collapsible sections replaced from CSS triangle to genuine Heroicon.</li>
680: </ul>
681: <h3>Fixed</h3>
682: <ul>
683: <li>Web UI: loading spinners now centered in settings pane, diff panel, and file previews.</li>
684: <li>Web UI: Tavily and Brave Search input fields aligned to equal widths.</li>
685: <li>Web UI: SSH hosts form reordered — password field before key field.</li>
686: </ul>
687: <h2>0.9.6</h2>
688: <h3>Internal</h3>
689: <ul>
690: <li>Removed unused <code>formatActiveRulesPrompt</code> — the per-turn rules path has used <code>formatRulesForTurn</code> (single combined <code>&lt;rules&gt;</code> block) since it was introduced; the legacy two-part formatter had no callers outside its own tests.</li>
691: </ul>
692: <h2>0.9.5</h2>
693: <h3>Added</h3>
694: <ul>
695: <li>Two new built-in personas: <code>researcher</code> (web-search-driven investigation, cites sources) and <code>assistant</code> (general-purpose everyday help — advice, quick lookups, drafts — that reaches for tools only when a task actually needs them).</li>
696: <li>Web UI: the Files panel&#39;s <code>.md</code> preview now renders through a real markdown engine (headings, lists, tables, links) and code files get real per-language syntax highlighting, both vendored for fully offline use. The Settings → Skills &quot;read full content&quot; view got the same treatment, in the same size modal as the file preview.</li>
697: <li>Web UI: every finished agent reply now shows its own &quot;provider · model · Ns&quot; footer, persisted per-turn — a thread with several exchanges shows a footer under each one, not just whichever was most recent, and it survives a full page reload.</li>
698: </ul>
699: <h3>Fixed</h3>
700: <ul>
701: <li>Web UI: a disabled plugin&#39;s skill still worked as a native slash command and stayed listed in the composer palette — both now correctly disappear.</li>
702: <li>TUI: <code>/plugin</code> silently cloned three GitHub-hosted default marketplaces on first use with no way to tell where they came from. They&#39;re back as permanent, always-present catalogs (labeled &quot;built-in&quot; in the web UI), but non-removable and no longer a surprise — <code>/plugin marketplace add</code> is the documented way to add your own.</li>
703: <li>Web UI: Chinese trigger phrases removed from three built-in skill descriptions; the command palette now truncates a long description with an ellipsis instead of letting it overflow the row.</li>
704: <li>Web UI: clicking a file&#39;s icon or the empty space in its row (not just the filename text) now opens its preview, matching the whole row&#39;s hover/click-target styling.</li>
705: <li>Web UI: fixed the Files preview&#39;s markdown spacing (was inheriting the chat&#39;s pre-wrap styling, doubling up as huge line gaps), added Escape-to-close, and removed a raw-then-rendered flash on a slow connection.</li>
706: <li>Web UI: the stale &quot;provider · model · Ns&quot; footer and elapsed-time counter from a just-finished session no longer bleed into a brand-new session.</li>
707: <li>Web UI: centered &quot;Loading…&quot; states that were pinned top-left instead of filling their container (Settings tabs, Status popover, Files panel&#39;s initial load).</li>
708: <li>Web UI: a hand-approximated <code>chevronUp</code> icon path was fixed to match its actual Heroicons source.</li>
709: </ul>
710: <h2>0.9.4</h2>
711: <h3>Added</h3>
712: <ul>
713: <li>A loaded skill can now be invoked as a native <code>/&lt;skill-id&gt;</code> slash command in both the terminal and web composer — it shows up in autocomplete with its own description, no <code>/skill:name</code> prefix needed. <code>/reload</code> (and enabling/disabling a skill in the web Settings modal) refreshes the list immediately.</li>
714: </ul>
715: <h3>Fixed</h3>
