prompts/error-handling.md:7:- All bash commands must be non-interactive — they run without a TTY and cannot receive stdin. Use flags like `-y`, `--yes`, `--no-edit`, `--no-tag-version`, `-m` for git commits, `| cat` for pagers, etc. Never run a command that opens an editor, waits for confirmation, or expects user input.
